# Desktop routing — SELKIES stack. Provisioned at build time into
# /etc/caddy/desktop.d/ and glob-imported by the main Caddyfile when
# DESKTOP_STACK includes selkies. Owns /desktop/ (runs parallel to /vnc/).
#
# Selkies 2.x serves its web client AND its WebSocket (/desktop/api/websockets) and a small API
# from one HTTP server on 127.0.0.1:6080, under the path prefix it is started with
# (--subfolder=/desktop, see etc/desktop/start-selkies.sh). So the whole /desktop/ tree is one
# reverse proxy with no path rewriting: the client builds its WebSocket address from the URL it was
# loaded from. (Selkies 1.x was WebSocket-only and Caddy served its static client; both are gone.)
#
# AUTH: everything under /desktop/ is behind the UNIFIED AUTH GATEWAY (the forward_auth session
# gate in the main Caddyfile runs before this snippet), the client, the API and the WebSocket
# alike; the session cookie rides the WS upgrade. Selkies has no login of its own and needs none:
# its Basic auth is switched off and it listens on loopback only. Do NOT re-add a basic_auth here:
# it cannot gate the JS WebSocket and would only add a redundant prompt.
#
# Caddy's reverse_proxy keeps the Host header, which is what Selkies compares a WebSocket's Origin
# with (a cross-site page is refused with 403), and upgrades WebSockets by itself.

handle /desktop/* {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:6080 {
		flush_interval -1
	}
}
handle /desktop {
	redir /desktop/ permanent
}
